 'Charter pillar: security. Metric turnstile_on_public_forms (bp26_probe_results subjects qnfo.org#ld-sub-form, papers.qnfo.org#ld-sub-form, papers.qnfo.org#ask-f). Doer: qnfo-gateway via qnfo-code-orchestrator. Copy the marked block between "// BEGIN TURNSTILE-EDGE-1" and "// END TURNSTILE-EDGE-1" from scripts/turnstile-edge.snippet.js (scripts/turnstile-edge.test.mjs asserts the copy is verbatim and lists the workers: add qnfo-gateway there). Render turnstileWidget(env, "gateway_subscribe") plus TURNSTILE_SCRIPT inside the ld-sub-form markup (both copies) and inside the ask-f form; the page script sends cf_turnstile (the cf-turnstile-response input of the form) in the JSON body to /api/subscribe; handleSubscribeProxy calls turnstileVerify(env, body.cf_turnstile, CF-Connecting-IP, null) before it forwards to qnfo-subscribers (pass a null action: ask.qwav.tech posts here too, with action ask_subscribe, and ideas/ipatent verify their own). qnfo-gateway already lists TURNSTILE_SECRET as a worker secret in its wrangler.toml (the living-paper widget on papers.qnfo.org, sitekey 0x4AAAAADdymctNL1u4zXpJ); the new widget qnfo-edge-forms-1 (sitekey 0x4AAAAAAFpf2WdSG4-h5mu_) covers qnfo.org and papers.qnfo.org, so do not rotate the existing secret: set the new one only through the secret lock (docs/BP26-EDGE-SECURITY-1.md). Fail-open only while the secret is unbound. Bump the minor VERSION and keep deployed-current.worker.js identical. Closing probe: bp26_probe_results turnstile_on_public_forms rows for those three subjects flip to ok on the next collector run.
